description: Trigger ONLY when the user provides the result set of an already-executed
  Cortex XSIAM XQL query and asks to extract, pull, or list the indicators of compromise
  from it. Accepts results as a rendered table (headers such as _time and event_type
  plus rows), JSON row objects, or CSV. The skill reads the rows, identifies IPv4
  and IPv6 addresses, domains, URLs, file hashes (MD5, SHA1, SHA256), email addresses,
  and file paths, deduplicates them, and returns a formatted Markdown table grouped
  by indicator type for threat-intel lookup. The output is always a written Markdown
  table. Do NOT activate to write or run XQL, summarize the narrative of the logs,
  assign threat verdicts, or recommend response actions.
